    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37872" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-pūtĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n.
		vox hibr., prae<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσθιον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
			foreskin</i>, <i>prepuce.</i>—In
				plur., <i><span class="en">Juv. 6, 238</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 99</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Apoc. 8, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen. 17, 11</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: circumcidite praeputium cordis
			vestri, <i>do away with impurity</i>, Laet. 4, 17, 8;
				<i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Jer. 4, 4</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the retaining of
				the prepuce</i>, <i>uncircumcision</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gal. 5,
				6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Eph. 2, 11</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
